    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DxL9d5fu37W3m3zsfHHvEv)_\n\n**Why the error came back:** #101 changed `sp-env.el` only. The `.el` is tangled from `docs/tangles/base/sp-env.org`, which still had the old code, so the tangle in ffe0ae9 restored it (the top-level `dolist` with `...` calling `exec-path-from-shell-copy-env` before the package is loaded).\n\n**Fix:** the same change, now in the org source and in the `.el`: `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` joins the list in the `use-package` `:config`; the daemon case is in the `:if` condition; the two top-level forms and their doc sections are removed. CHANGELOG and the doc's \"Changes by pull request\" updated.\n\n**Not tested:** no Emacs in the container, so I could not run `tools/check-tangle.sh` or start Emacs. The `.el` was edited by the same replacements as the org blocks; please run the check or re-tangle.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01VmpaH7h5GRXDBJYjUQKtJQ)_",
    "changed_files": 3,
